From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:46:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: no watchdog work for a radio that isn't
 running

mt7915_mac_work() re-arms itself each time, and mt7915_stop() cancels
it. An L1 recovery and reconfig_complete() queue it for both radios,
though, and a radio with no interface up was never started, so it is
never stopped either. From the first recovery on, the work ran for that
radio for good: a channel query to the firmware twice a second under the
device mutex, the MIB counters and the noise floor read from a radio
that isn't on, and nothing to cancel it when the driver is unloaded.

It returns without re-arming when its radio isn't running.

mt7915_test_mac_work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c            | 12 ++++++++++++
 mt7915/tests/mac-test.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index 7f210368..fea311ec 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -2231,6 +2231,18 @@ void mt7915_mac_work(struct work_struct *work)
 
 	mutex_lock(&mphy->dev->mutex);
 
+	/*
+	 * An L1 recovery and a restart queue this for both radios, a stopped
+	 * one too (mt7915_stop() cancels it, but a radio with no interface
+	 * was never started). It has nothing to watch there, and re-arming
+	 * itself would query the firmware for it twice a second from then on,
+	 * with nothing left to cancel it when the driver is unloaded.
+	 */
+	if (!test_bit(MT76_STATE_RUNNING, &mphy->state)) {
+		mutex_unlock(&mphy->dev->mutex);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * Each firmware query holds the mutex for a round trip, so they're
 	 * spaced out: the channel's airtime every 500 ms (its counters are
diff --git a/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c b/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
index d44b6268..39bf6e94 100644
--- a/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
+++ b/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
@@ -5355,7 +5355,7 @@ static void mt7915_test_muru_reply(struct mt76_test_fake *fake,
 
 /* The watchdog work, every 100 ms: the noise floor each time; every 5th
  * time the channel survey, the MIB counters and the rx-stuck checks; every
- * 100th (when enabled) the MU stats. It always re-arms itself.
+ * 100th (when enabled) the MU stats. It re-arms itself while its radio runs.
  */
 static void mt7915_test_mac_work(struct kunit *test)
 {
@@ -5427,6 +5427,22 @@ static void mt7915_test_mac_work(struct kunit *test)
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt76_test_count_msgs(fake,
 			MCU_EXT_CMD(MURU_CTRL)), 1);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dev->phy.muru_work_count, 0);
+
+	/* A stopped radio (or one never started: an L1 recovery and a restart
+	 * queue the work for both) has nothing to watch: no query, and the work
+	 * doesn't keep itself going.
+	 */
+	clear_bit(MT76_STATE_RUNNING, &dev->mphy.state);
+	for (i = 0; i < 5; i++)
+		mt7915_mac_work(&dev->mphy.mac_work.work);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, delayed_work_pending(&dev->mphy.mac_work));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dev->mphy.mac_work_count, 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt76_test_count_msgs(fake,
+			MCU_EXT_CMD(GET_MIB_INFO)), 20);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, mutex_is_locked(&dev->mt76.mutex));
+	/* nothing is left to run after the test, whatever it found */
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dev->mphy.mac_work);
+	set_bit(MT76_STATE_RUNNING, &dev->mphy.state);
 }
 
 /* A complete SER (L1) recovery: DMA stopped and reset, tokens reclaimed,
